-- title:
--   Miracle flatness for a local map of regular local rings
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings, each a regular local ring in the sense of Mathlib's `IsRegularLocalRing` (with $S$ in addition carrying a Noetherian ring instance), and let $S$ be an $R$-algebra whose structure map $\operatorname{algebraMap} R S$ is a local homomorphism, i.e. it pulls back non-units to non-units, so that the maximal ideal of $R$ maps into that of $S$. Assume two numerical hypotheses, both on Krull dimensions taken in $\mathrm{WithBot}\,\mathbb{N}_\infty$: first, the closed fibre $S/\mathfrak{m}_R S$, that is the quotient of $S$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak{m}_R = \mathrm{maximalIdeal}\,R$ under $\operatorname{algebraMap} R S$, has $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} = 0$; and second, $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} S = \operatorname{ringKrullDim} R$. The conclusion is that $S$ is flat as an $R$-module, `Module.Flat R S`. No finiteness of $S$ over $R$ is assumed: the result is the purely ring-theoretic form of miracle flatness, with the zero-dimensionality of the closed fibre in place of a module-finiteness hypothesis, and $R$, $S$ are allowed to lie in different universes.
--
--   This is the classical miracle-flatness criterion for a local homomorphism of regular local rings: equality of dimensions together with a zero-dimensional closed fibre forces flatness. It is used in the project's geometric flatness statements, where the stalk map of a locally quasi-finite morphism from a smooth (hence locally regular) scheme has zero-dimensional fibre, yielding finiteness and flatness of such morphisms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_Flat_of_isLocalHom_of_isRegularLocalRing_of_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_zero.lean

